\par\b\fs28 \u167?4 Sources round\b0\fs24\par


\par Van de Giessen does not cover Leviticus (does cover Genesis 1\u8211?25 and Deut. 18\u8211?34); the witnesses were verified via Sefaria.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222?/\u-10179?\u-8223? \b Azazel (16:8) \u8212? four lines.\b0  (a) Peshat/translation: \u8220?the goat that goes away / is sent away\u8221? \u8212? so the LXX read it (apopompaios), and so \u8220?scapegoat\u8221? (KJV) \u-10179?\u-8222?; this carries the \u8220?carried away\u8221? motif. (b) Place: a hard, steep mountain/cliff (Yoma; Saadiah Gaon: a mountain name) \u-10179?\u-8223?. (c) Wilderness power: Ibn Ezra hides a \u8220?secret\u8221? (\u8220?when you are 33 you will know it\u8221?); Ramban decodes it as a demonic power \u8212? with the emphatic guard that the goat is not an offering to that power, but is sent at God\u8217?s command to its domain, while the atonement is made \u8220?before the LORD\u8221? \u-10179?\u-8223?. (d) Aggada: Uzza/Azael, the fallen \u8220?sons of God\u8221? (Yoma 67b) \u-10179?\u-8223?.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Chok (Yoma 67b / Lev. 18:4).\b0  The sent-away goat stands among the statutes that \u8220?the satan\u8221? and the nations mock as irrational; \u8220?I am the LORD, I decreed it.\u8221? Discipline note: the rite is a decree, not a rationalisable mechanism \u8212? red against over-explanation.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b \u8220?Before the face\u8221? (16:30; Yoma).\b0  \u8220?lifnei HaShem tit'haru\u8221? \u8212? becoming clean happens before Him; in the Temple service priests and people fell down at hearing the pronounced Name. Anchors the day\u8217?s title.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8907? \b Hebrews 9\u8211?10 (confessional).\b0  Yeshua enters the true sanctuary once by His own blood and appears \u8220?in the presence of God for us\u8221? (9:12,24). Horizon, not flat typology: the pattern (priest, blood, access, atonement) points; it does not settle the peshat of Leviticus 16.\par


\par \u9898? \b Onkelos\b0  on 16:8 (Azazel as a place?): still to be verified.\par


\par \b Revision gate.\b0  Did the round shift the centre? Confirming and sharpening: the peshat \u8220?sent away\u8221? carries Source/carrying-away; the chok note guards against over-explaining; and \u8220?before the face\u8221? anchors the centre \u8212? without letting the reflex become flat surrender.\par



\par\b\fs28 \u167?5 Direction test as horizon\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8907? Confessional. Matthew 25 tests the fruit of received atonement: whoever has truly stood before God\u8217?s face cannot let the hungry, the stranger and the prisoner become invisible \u8212? \u8220?what you did for the least, you did for Me.\u8221? And Hebrews 9\u8211?10 confesses Yeshua as the High Priest who opened the way. \u-10179?\u-8908? Guarded: Matt. 25 and Heb. 9\u8211?10 do not settle the peshat of Leviticus 16; both are horizon. And the turn to the neighbour is fruit, not price \u8212? Lev. 16 stands: the atonement comes first from God.\par



